    "https://twitter.com/WSUCareers": {
      "title": "Westfield State Career Center",
      "description": "Westfield State Career Center (@WSUCareers) / X Log in Sign up Westfield State Career Center 3,531 posts Westfield State Career Center @WSUCareers Career advising for students and alumni of Westfield State University Westfield, MA careers.westfield.ma.edu Joined March 2009 2,034 Following 1,944 Followers Mention Follow Posts Posts Replies Replies Reposts Reposts Media Media Log in or sign up for X See what’s happening and join the conversation Continue with phone Continue with Apple Continue with Google or Log in with username or email Terms · Privacy · Cookies · Accessibility · US TIDA · Ads Info · More © 2026 X Corp. Westfield State Career Center @WSUCareers Mar 13, 2023 The Job & Internship Fair will be Wednesday, March 29 from 1-3:30 PM in Scanlon Banquet Hall! For a complete list of employers, visit westfield.joinhandshake.com/login?requeste… 2 2 409 Westfield State Career Center @WSUCareers Nov 1, 2022 Students: Got plans for winter break? Check out the #EACE Virtual Road Trips to the Real World program! Registration is NOW OPEN! eace.org/roadtrips Westfield State Career Center @WSUCareers Mar 21, 2022 Client Administrator Job Opportunity with @ MarkESalomone - Send Resume and Cover Letter to Odete Tome-Wells  at [email protected] Westfield State Career Center @WSUCareers Mar 10, 2022 Register for the @ ebcne Environmental, Energy, and Engineering Career Fair on April 11 from 4:30 - 6:30 PM in Boston, MA! Environmental, Energy, and Engineering Career Fair - Environmental Business Council of New England,... From ebcne.org Westfield State Career Center @WSUCareers Feb 23, 2022 ONE MONTH until the Virtual Job + Internship Fair! \n\n📣 90+ employers!\n💻 Register online at westfield.joinhandshake.com Don’t miss this opportunity to network with employers. Sign up for group and 1:1 sessions before they fill up! \n\n🎨 design by: Robert W., intern"
    },
    "https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/staff/": {
      "title": "Meet The Team",
      "description": "Meet The Team – Career Center | Westfield State University Class of 2025, take our Post-Graduate Outcomes Survey to let us know where you landed after WSU! Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Career Center Instagram LinkedIn Pinterest X (formerly Twitter) YouTube Schedule an Appointment Donate Students & Alumni Explore Career Pathways Discovery & Exploration Job Trends & Salaries Arts, Media, Marketing & Communications Business Management Counseling & Social Justice Criminal Justice, Government & Law Education Finance & Accounting Health & Fitness Information Technology Science & Math Additional Resources for Students Job Boards, Networking & Career Support Employers Employer Sponsorship Register for a Career Fair Recruiting Options Faculty & Staff Career Champions Prospective Students WSU Career Fairs & Events Meet the Team Meet The Team Mission: The Westfield State University Career Center empowers all students to explore, prepare for, and achieve meaningful careers by providing equitable access to personalized guidance, experiential learning, and strategic partnerships that reflect the evolving global workforce and promote lifelong professional success. Vision: To empower all students—regardless of background—to achieve meaningful careers by providing equitable access to career education, experiential learning, and strategic partnerships with employers and the community. Junior Delgado Giselle Frechette Dino Innarelli Sharon Welch Lori Putnam Chelsea Rose-Dunham Sarah Kraft Junior Delgado Director Junior Delgado presently serves as the Director of the Career Center at Westfield State University (MA) and has been in that role since 2009. Junior is also the The Washington Center Program Coordinator. As a first-generation college graduate and bilingual speaker, (English/Spanish), he has worked in higher education for over 20 years in career services and a short time in Admissions. He has been focused on serving student populations to achieve their goals over the course of his career. Junior recently completed a year long term as the President of the Eastern Association of Colleges and Employers (EACE): an organization dedicated to connecting career counseling professionals with the employer community. Additionally, over the last ten years he has served as the Executive Chair/President to the Massachusetts Educational Recruiting Consortium (MERC); an organization that facilitates hiring in Education. Contact Phone Number 413-572-5206 Location Parenzo Hall 130 Email jdelgado@westfield.ma.edu LinkedIn @juniordelgado Schedule an Appointment View Calendar 413-572-5206 Recent Posts Labor Market Insights Module Giselle Frechette Associate Director Giselle Frechette joined the Westfield State University Career Center in February 2007 and has over 20 years of experience in the field.  Giselle serves as the Disney College Program Advisor. As a first-generation college graduate, Giselle is committed to helping students navigate college, understand the various career pathways, and make professional connections to reach their personal and professional goals.  Her passion is helping students get connected to the right opportunities to find their life’s passion. If you have an opportunity for a student or a recent graduate, she’d love to connect you with the right candidate! Go Owls! Contact Phone Number 413-572-5206 Location Parenzo Hall 130 Email gfrechette@westfield.ma.edu LinkedIn @gisellefrechette Schedule an Appointment View Calendar 413-572-5206 Recent Posts Advice from Graduates (2:54) What I Wish I Knew (3:09) Early Career Programs & Internships for College Students Find Mentors Make Your Resume Pop (3:31) Dino Innarelli Assistant Director and Coordinator of Data Management and Alumni Career Services Dino joined the Career Center in 2010 with over twenty years of career advising and workforce development experience.  He manages the data collection, analysis, and reporting process; Professional Networking Nights; the Annual Post Graduate Report, and facilitates other Career Center programming. Dino also provides career development and graduate school advising, responds to data requests from various schools and departments across the university, and has served on several search committees. He holds STRONG and CDF (Career Development Facilitator) certifications as well as a bachelor’s degree from Western New England University and a Master of Public Administration from Westfield State University. Contact Phone Number 413-572-5206 Location Parenzo Hall 130 Email dinnarelli@westfield.ma.edu LinkedIn Connect on LinkedIn Schedule an Appointment View Calendar 413-572-5206 Sharon Welch Administrative Assistant II Sharon joined the WSU Career Center in 1999 after 15 years of professional experience in the banking industry.  Her contributions to this busy student support service office include program planning and development, marketing, and financial and office management.  She enjoys working with students, employers and the University community to help prepare students for successful careers and advanced study. Contact Phone Number 413-572-5206 Location Parenzo Hall 130 Email swelch@westfield.ma.edu LinkedIn Connect on LinkedIn Lori Putnam Clerk IV Lori joined the Career Center in August 2008 after thirty years in corporate America.  Her contributions to the Career Center include posting jobs in Handshake, connecting with employers, managing databases as well as training and supervising student workers to aid in their professional development.  She enjoys welcoming students and visitors to the office and discussing Career Center resources.  Lori often volunteers at University events to contribute to the overall success of the institution.  Lori has completed coursework in Liberal Studies and Legal Secretarial at Fitchburg State University and Springfield Technical Community College.  Lori is also pursuing her undergraduate degree. Contact Phone Number 413-572-5206 Location Parenzo Hall 130 Email lputnam@westfield.ma.edu LinkedIn @lori-putnam-23872431 Chelsea Rose-Dunham Employer Relations Associate & Career Counselor Chelsea Rose-Dunham is the Employer Relations Associate and Career Counselor in the Career Center at Westfield State University, a role she began in August 2026. With more than a decade of experience spanning employer relations, career development, student engagement, and higher education, Chelsea is dedicated to building meaningful connections between students and employers. Before joining Westfield State, she spent 10 years at Emmanuel College in Boston, advancing through four progressive employer engagement roles before serving as Senior Associate Director of Employer Engagement. In that position, she led strategic employer partnership initiatives, launched innovative recruitment programs, expanded internship and experiential learning opportunities, and strengthened campus recruitment efforts that significantly increased both employer participation and student engagement. Throughout her career, Chelsea has been passionate about creating equitable pathways to career success and helping students confidently navigate their professional journeys. Beyond career services, Chelsea served as an Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach at Emmanuel College for eight seasons, mentoring student-athletes while contributing to multiple conference championships and NCAA Tournament appearances. Her diverse professional background also includes supporting young learners in early education, working in retail sales and customer relations, coordinating art exhibitions and gallery operations, along with hospitality and service-focused environments. These experiences have strengthened her commitment to relationship building, customer service, and creating meaningful connections that help individuals navigate their personal and professional goals. Chelsea holds a Bachelor of Arts in History with a minor in Art History from Southern New Hampshire University and is committed to empowering students to explore career possibilities, build professional relationships, and work towards their goals. Contact Phone Number 413-572-8166 Location Parenzo Hall - Room 130 Email crosedunham@westfield.ma.edu Website westfield.joinhandshake.com/edu/schools/563 LinkedIn @chelsearosedunham Sarah Kraft Graduate Assistant Sarah Kraft is the current Graduate Assistant at the Career Center. Through her academic and professional experiences, she has had the opportunity to work with individuals from diverse backgrounds and with a variety of needs and experiences. Sarah earned her Bachelor of Science in Psychology from Springfield College in 2023 and is currently pursuing her Master of Social Work at Westfield State University. In addition to her role at the Career Center, she works full-time as a Therapeutic Mentor at Gándara Mental Health Center, where she provides individualized support to youth by helping them develop coping skills, build positive social and interpersonal skills, work toward personal goals, and navigate challenges in their daily lives. Sarah is passionate about helping students explore life after college, identify and achieve their personal and professional goals, and feel confident in their next steps. She strives to create a welcoming, supportive, and safe space where students can ask questions, explore their interests, and feel empowered as they prepare for their future. Contact Email skraft@westfield.ma.edu LinkedIn @sarah-kraft-a5b53a27a Contact & Location Phone 413-572-5206 Email careers@westfield.ma.edu Website https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/ Address Westfield State University Parenzo Hall, 130 577 Western Avenue Westfield, MA 01086 Career Service Hours Day of the week Hours of Operation Summer Hours M Monday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm F Friday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm Meet the Team Junior Delgado Meet Junior Giselle Frechette Meet Giselle Dino Innarelli Meet Dino Sharon Welch Meet Sharon Lori Putnam Meet Lori Chelsea Rose-Dunham Meet Chelsea Sarah Kraft Meet Sarah Phone 413-572-5206 Email careers@westfield.ma.edu Website https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/ Address Westfield State University Parenzo Hall, 130 577 Western Avenue Westfield, MA 01086 Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Events Experiences Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Organizations Resources Meet the Team Instagram LinkedIn Pinterest X (formerly Twitter) YouTube Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Westfield State University"
    },
    "https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/channels/student/": {
      "title": "Students & Alumni",
      "description": "Students & Alumni – Career Center | Westfield State University Class of 2025, take our Post-Graduate Outcomes Survey to let us know where you landed after WSU! Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Career Center Instagram LinkedIn Pinterest X (formerly Twitter) YouTube Schedule an Appointment Donate Students & Alumni Explore Career Pathways Discovery & Exploration Job Trends & Salaries Arts, Media, Marketing & Communications Business Management Counseling & Social Justice Criminal Justice, Government & Law Education Finance & Accounting Health & Fitness Information Technology Science & Math Additional Resources for Students Job Boards, Networking & Career Support Employers Employer Sponsorship Register for a Career Fair Recruiting Options Faculty & Staff Career Champions Prospective Students WSU Career Fairs & Events Meet the Team Students & Alumni Career Exploration Resumes & Cover Letters Virtual Case Studies with Top Employers Internship Search Job Search Explore Job Market Hiring Trends Featured Opportunities Interview Prep Graduate School LinkedIn & Networking Explore Career Paths & Current Job Market Explore Hiring Employers & In-Demand Jobs Virtual Case Studies with Top Employers On-Campus Employment Skip filter options to posts Facing Career Fears: Video Series Filter Clear Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Blog Categories: Alumni Stories Career & Professional Development Advice Employer Spotlights Front Page News Guest Blog Industry Insights Student Stories Close Clear Filters Advice from Graduates (2:54) Share This: Share Advice from Graduates (2:54) on Facebook Share Advice from Graduates (2:54) on LinkedIn Share Advice from Graduates (2:54) on X Copy Link By Giselle Frechette Show author info Giselle Frechette Associate Director Send Email linkedin Read more » What I Wish I Knew (3:09) Share This: Share What I Wish I Knew (3:09) on Facebook Share What I Wish I Knew (3:09) on LinkedIn Share What I Wish I Knew (3:09) on X Copy Link By Giselle Frechette Show author info Giselle Frechette Associate Director Send Email linkedin Read more » Make Your Resume Pop (3:31) Share This: Share Make Your Resume Pop (3:31) on Facebook Share Make Your Resume Pop (3:31) on LinkedIn Share Make Your Resume Pop (3:31) on X Copy Link By Giselle Frechette Show author info Giselle Frechette Associate Director Send Email linkedin Read more » Sidebar Customize Email Alerts Explore Job Market Hiring Trends In partnership with Find a career that aligns with your career interests, see current salary projections, and identify skills you need to apply for that next job or internship. There are two ways to use this tool below: By Keyword: Search for the name of the occupation you’re interested in. By Industry: Not sure what job you’d like? Search by desired industry and see available occupations. Find career data by selecting keywords Keyword Search or, by filtering for industry and occupation Industry Search First, choose an industry of interest, then filter for occupation. (If you'd like to see data for a specific location only, filter by state.) Select an industry Select an industry Select an occupation Select an occupation Nationwide Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Nationwide/State Type in a keyword to select a relevant occupation. (If you'd like to see data for a specific location only, filter by state.) Search keyword Nationwide Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Nationwide/State Toggle charts 01 Occupation Description 02 Employment Trends 03 Top Employers 04 Education Levels 05 Annual Earnings 06 Technical Skills 07 Core Competencies 08 Job Titles Select data point Occupation Description Employment Trends Top Employers Education Levels Annual Earnings Technical Skills Core Competencies Job Titles Occupation Description Employment Trends The number of jobs in the career for the past two years, the current year, and projections for the next 10 years. Job counts include both employed and self-employed persons, and do not distinguish between full- and part-time jobs. Sources include Emsi industry data, staffing patterns, and OES data. Top Employers These companies are currently hiring for . Education Levels The educational attainment percentage breakdown for a career (e.g. the percentage of people in the career who hold Bachelor’s Degrees vs. Associate Degrees). Educational attainment levels are provided by O*NET. Annual Earnings Earnings figures are based on OES data from the BLS and include base rate, cost of living allowances, guaranteed pay, hazardous-duty pay, incentive pay (including commissions and bonuses), on-call pay, and tips. Technical Skills A list of hard skills associated with a given career ordered by the number of unique job postings which ask for those skills. Core Competencies The skills for the career. The \"importance\" is how relevant the ability is to the occupation: scale of 1-5. The \"level\" is the proficiency required by the occupation: scale of 0-100. Results are sorted by importance first, then level. Job Titles A list of job titles for all unique postings in a given career, sorted by frequency. Resume and Cover Letter Guides Skip filter options to posts Filter Clear Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Resource Categories: Career Paths by Major Employer Policies Featured Resources How-tos & Support Guides Interview Prep Resources Job Search Sites Networking Resources Online Tools Resume and Cover Letter Guides Westfield Handouts Close Clear Filters Federal Resume Handout Share This: Share Federal Resume Handout on Facebook Share Federal Resume Handout on LinkedIn Share Federal Resume Handout on X Copy Link View Resource Laboratory Skills for Resumes Share This: Share Laboratory Skills for Resumes on Facebook Share Laboratory Skills for Resumes on LinkedIn Share Laboratory Skills for Resumes on X Copy Link View Resource Cover Letter Sample 2 Share This: Share Cover Letter Sample 2 on Facebook Share Cover Letter Sample 2 on LinkedIn Share Cover Letter Sample 2 on X Copy Link View Sample Cover Letter Sample 1 Share This: Share Cover Letter Sample 1 on Facebook Share Cover Letter Sample 1 on LinkedIn Share Cover Letter Sample 1 on X Copy Link View Sample Teaching Resume Template Share This: Share Teaching Resume Template on Facebook Share Teaching Resume Template on LinkedIn Share Teaching Resume Template on X Copy Link Use this template as a guide to create your resume. Customize it to reflect your experiences, skills, and professional style. … Download Template STEM Resume Template Share This: Share STEM Resume Template on Facebook Share STEM Resume Template on LinkedIn Share STEM Resume Template on X Copy Link Use this template as a guide to create your resume. Customize it to reflect your experiences, skills, and professional style. … Download Template View All Resources LinkedIn & Networking Resources Skip filter options to posts Filter Clear Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Resource Categories: Career Paths by Major Employer Policies Featured