    "https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/channels/stem/": {
      "title": "Science & Math",
      "description": "Science & Math – Career Center | Westfield State University Class of 2025, take our Post-Graduate Outcomes Survey to let us know where you landed after WSU! Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Career Center Instagram LinkedIn Pinterest X (formerly Twitter) YouTube Schedule an Appointment Donate Students & Alumni Explore Career Pathways Discovery & Exploration Job Trends & Salaries Arts, Media, Marketing & Communications Business Management Counseling & Social Justice Criminal Justice, Government & Law Education Finance & Accounting Health & Fitness Information Technology Science & Math Additional Resources for Students Job Boards, Networking & Career Support Employers Employer Sponsorship Register for a Career Fair Recruiting Options Faculty & Staff Career Champions Prospective Students WSU Career Fairs & Events Meet the Team Science & Math Career Exploration Resumes & Cover Letters Virtual Case Studies with Top Employers Internship Search Job Search Explore Job Market Hiring Trends Featured Opportunities Interview Prep Graduate School LinkedIn & Networking Explore Career Paths & Current Job Market Explore Hiring Employers & In-Demand Jobs Virtual Case Studies with Top Employers On-Campus Employment Skip filter options to posts Facing Career Fears: Video Series Filter Clear Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Blog Categories: Alumni Stories Career & Professional Development Advice Employer Spotlights Front Page News Guest Blog Industry Insights Student Stories Close Clear Filters Advice from Graduates (2:54) Share This: Share Advice from Graduates (2:54) on Facebook Share Advice from Graduates (2:54) on LinkedIn Share Advice from Graduates (2:54) on X Copy Link By Giselle Frechette Show author info Giselle Frechette Associate Director Send Email linkedin Read more » What I Wish I Knew (3:09) Share This: Share What I Wish I Knew (3:09) on Facebook Share What I Wish I Knew (3:09) on LinkedIn Share What I Wish I Knew (3:09) on X Copy Link By Giselle Frechette Show author info Giselle Frechette Associate Director Send Email linkedin Read more » Make Your Resume Pop (3:31) Share This: Share Make Your Resume Pop (3:31) on Facebook Share Make Your Resume Pop (3:31) on LinkedIn Share Make Your Resume Pop (3:31) on X Copy Link By Giselle Frechette Show author info Giselle Frechette Associate Director Send Email linkedin Read more » Sidebar Customize Email Alerts Upcoming Events March Mar 02 Event: USPS Hiring Event Portsmouth NH -every Monday Mon, Mar 2 at 10am - Mon, Sep 28 at 4pm Monday, March 2nd at 10am - Monday, September 28th at 4pm April Apr 03 Event: USPS Hiring Event Portland ME every Friday Fri, Apr 3 at 10am - Fri, Sep 25 at 4pm Friday, April 3rd at 10am - Friday, September 25th at 4pm September Sep 04 Event: Register Here: 2026 SMBC Explore (for College Sophomores) Fri, Sep 4 from 10am - 4pm Friday, September 4th from 10am - 4pm Sep 08 Event: GWI Ask Admissions: Open Q&A Session Tue, Sep 8 from 4pm - 4:45pm Tuesday, September 8th from 4pm - 4:45pm Sep 08 Event: Kraft Heinz 101: Session 1 Tue, Sep 8 from 5pm - 6pm Tuesday, September 8th from 5pm - 6pm View More Explore Job Market Hiring Trends In partnership with Find a career that aligns with your career interests, see current salary projections, and identify skills you need to apply for that next job or internship. There are two ways to use this tool below: By Keyword: Search for the name of the occupation you’re interested in. By Industry: Not sure what job you’d like? Search by desired industry and see available occupations. Find career data by selecting keywords Keyword Search or, by filtering for industry and occupation Industry Search First, choose an industry of interest, then filter for occupation. (If you'd like to see data for a specific location only, filter by state.) Select an industry Select an industry Select an occupation Select an occupation Nationwide Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Nationwide/State Type in a keyword to select a relevant occupation. (If you'd like to see data for a specific location only, filter by state.) Search keyword Nationwide Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Nationwide/State Toggle charts 01 Occupation Description 02 Employment Trends 03 Top Employers 04 Education Levels 05 Annual Earnings 06 Technical Skills 07 Core Competencies 08 Job Titles Select data point Occupation Description Employment Trends Top Employers Education Levels Annual Earnings Technical Skills Core Competencies Job Titles Occupation Description Employment Trends The number of jobs in the career for the past two years, the current year, and projections for the next 10 years. Job counts include both employed and self-employed persons, and do not distinguish between full- and part-time jobs. Sources include Emsi industry data, staffing patterns, and OES data. Top Employers These companies are currently hiring for . Education Levels The educational attainment percentage breakdown for a career (e.g. the percentage of people in the career who hold Bachelor’s Degrees vs. Associate Degrees). Educational attainment levels are provided by O*NET. Annual Earnings Earnings figures are based on OES data from the BLS and include base rate, cost of living allowances, guaranteed pay, hazardous-duty pay, incentive pay (including commissions and bonuses), on-call pay, and tips. Technical Skills A list of hard skills associated with a given career ordered by the number of unique job postings which ask for those skills. Core Competencies The skills for the career. The \"importance\" is how relevant the ability is to the occupation: scale of 1-5. The \"level\" is the proficiency required by the occupation: scale of 0-100. Results are sorted by importance first, then level. Job Titles A list of job titles for all unique postings in a given career, sorted by frequency. Resume and Cover Letter Guides Skip filter options to posts Filter Clear Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Resource Categories: Career Paths by Major Employer Policies Featured Resources How-tos & Support Guides Interview Prep Resources Job Search Sites Networking Resources Online Tools Resume and Cover Letter Guides Westfield Handouts Close Clear Filters Federal Resume Handout Share This: Share Federal Resume Handout on Facebook Share Federal Resume Handout on LinkedIn Share Federal Resume Handout on X Copy Link View Resource Laboratory Skills for Resumes Share This: Share Laboratory Skills for Resumes on Facebook Share Laboratory Skills for Resumes on LinkedIn Share Laboratory Skills for Resumes on X Copy Link View Resource Cover Letter Sample 2 Share This: Share Cover Letter Sample 2 on Facebook Share Cover Letter Sample 2 on LinkedIn Share Cover Letter Sample 2 on X Copy Link View Sample Cover Letter Sample 1 Share This: Share Cover Letter Sample 1 on Facebook Share Cover Letter Sample 1 on LinkedIn Share Cover Letter Sample 1 on X Copy Link View Sample Teaching Resume Template Share This: Share Teaching Resume Template on Facebook Share Teaching Resu