and reporting process; Professional Networking Nights; the Annual Post Graduate Report, and facilitates other Career Center programming. Dino also provides career development and graduate school advising, responds to data requests from various schools and departments across the university, and has served on several search committees. He holds STRONG and CDF (Career Development Facilitator) certifications as well as a bachelor’s degree from Western New England University and a Master of Public Administration from Westfield State University. Contact Phone Number 413-572-5206 Location Parenzo Hall 130 Email dinnarelli@westfield.ma.edu LinkedIn Connect on LinkedIn Schedule an Appointment View Calendar 413-572-5206 Sharon Welch Administrative Assistant II Sharon joined the WSU Career Center in 1999 after 15 years of professional experience in the banking industry.  Her contributions to this busy student support service office include program planning and development, marketing, and financial and office management.  She enjoys working with students, employers and the University community to help prepare students for successful careers and advanced study. Contact Phone Number 413-572-5206 Location Parenzo Hall 130 Email swelch@westfield.ma.edu LinkedIn Connect on LinkedIn Lori Putnam Clerk IV Lori joined the Career Center in August 2008 after thirty years in corporate America.  Her contributions to the Career Center include posting jobs in Handshake, connecting with employers, managing databases as well as training and supervising student workers to aid in their professional development.  She enjoys welcoming students and visitors to the office and discussing Career Center resources.  Lori often volunteers at University events to contribute to the overall success of the institution.  Lori has completed coursework in Liberal Studies and Legal Secretarial at Fitchburg State University and Springfield Technical Community College.  Lori is also pursuing her undergraduate degree. Contact Phone Number 413-572-5206 Location Parenzo Hall 130 Email lputnam@westfield.ma.edu LinkedIn @lori-putnam-23872431 Chelsea Rose-Dunham Employer Relations Associate & Career Counselor Chelsea Rose-Dunham is the Employer Relations Associate and Career Counselor in the Career Center at Westfield State University, a role she began in August 2026. With more than a decade of experience spanning employer relations, career development, student engagement, and higher education, Chelsea is dedicated to building meaningful connections between students and employers. Before joining Westfield State, she spent 10 years at Emmanuel College in Boston, advancing through four progressive employer engagement roles before serving as Senior Associate Director of Employer Engagement. In that position, she led strategic employer partnership initiatives, launched innovative recruitment programs, expanded internship and experiential learning opportunities, and strengthened campus recruitment efforts that significantly increased both employer participation and student engagement. Throughout her career, Chelsea has been passionate about creating equitable pathways to career success and helping students confidently navigate their professional journeys. Beyond career services, Chelsea served as an Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach at Emmanuel College for eight seasons, mentoring student-athletes while contributing to multiple conference championships and NCAA Tournament appearances. Her diverse professional background also includes supporting young learners in early education, working in retail sales and customer relations, coordinating art exhibitions and gallery operations, along with hospitality and service-focused environments. These experiences have strengthened her commitment to relationship building, customer service, and creating meaningful connections that help individuals navigate their personal and professional goals. Chelsea holds a Bachelor of Arts in History with a minor in Art History from Southern New Hampshire University and is committed to empowering students to explore career possibilities, build professional relationships, and work towards their goals. Contact Phone Number 413-572-8166 Location Parenzo Hall - Room 130 Email crosedunham@westfield.ma.edu Website westfield.joinhandshake.com/edu/schools/563 LinkedIn @chelsearosedunham Sarah Kraft Graduate Assistant Sarah Kraft is the current Graduate Assistant at the Career Center. Through her academic and professional experiences, she has had the opportunity to work with individuals from diverse backgrounds and with a variety of needs and experiences. Sarah earned her Bachelor of Science in Psychology from Springfield College in 2023 and is currently pursuing her Master of Social Work at Westfield State University. In addition to her role at the Career Center, she works full-time as a Therapeutic Mentor at Gándara Mental Health Center, where she provides individualized support to youth by helping them develop coping skills, build positive social and interpersonal skills, work toward personal goals, and navigate challenges in their daily lives. Sarah is passionate about helping students explore life after college, identify and achieve their personal and professional goals, and feel confident in their next steps. She strives to create a welcoming, supportive, and safe space where students can ask questions, explore their interests, and feel empowered as they prepare for their future. Contact Email skraft@westfield.ma.edu LinkedIn @sarah-kraft-a5b53a27a Contact & Location Phone 413-572-5206 Email careers@westfield.ma.edu Website https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/ Address Westfield State University Parenzo Hall, 130 577 Western Avenue Westfield, MA 01086 Career Service Hours Day of the week Hours of Operation Summer Hours M Monday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm F Friday 8:30 am- 4:30 pm 8:00 am- 4:00 pm Meet the Team Junior Delgado Meet Junior Giselle Frechette Meet Giselle Dino Innarelli Meet Dino Sharon Welch Meet Sharon Lori Putnam Meet Lori Chelsea Rose-Dunham Meet Chelsea Sarah Kraft Meet Sarah Phone 413-572-5206 Email careers@westfield.ma.edu Website https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/ Address Westfield State University Parenzo Hall, 130 577 Western Avenue Westfield, MA 01086 Footer Column 1 Alumni Connections Events Experiences Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Organizations Resources Meet the Team Instagram LinkedIn Pinterest X (formerly Twitter) YouTube Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Westfield State University"
    },
    "https://careers.westfield.ma.edu/staff/#lori-putnam": {
      "title": "Meet The Team",
      "description": "Meet The Team – Career Center | Westfield State University Class of 2025, take our Post-Graduate Outcomes Survey to let us know where you landed after WSU! Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Career Center Instagram LinkedIn Pinterest X (formerly Twitter) YouTube Schedule an Appointment Donate Students & Alumni Explore Career Pathways Discovery & Exploration Job Trends & Salaries Arts, Media, Marketing & Communications Business Management Counseling & Social Justice Criminal Justice, Government & Law Education Finance & Accounting Health & Fitness Information Technology Science & Math Additional Resources for Students Job Boards, Networking & Career Support Employers Employer Sponsorship Register for a Career Fair Recruiting Options Faculty & Staff Career Champions Prospective Students WSU Career Fairs & Events Meet the Team Meet The Team Mission: The Westfield State University Career Center empowers all students to explore, prepare for, and achieve meaningful careers by providing equitable access to personalized guidance, experiential learning, and strategic partnerships that reflect the evolving global workforce and promote lifelong professional success. Vision: To empower all students—regardless of background—to achieve meaningful careers by providing equitable access to career education, experiential learning, and strategic partnerships with employers and the community. Junior Delgado Giselle Frechette Dino Innarelli Sharon Welch Lori Putnam Chelsea Rose-Dunham Sarah Kraft Junior Delgado Director Junior Delgado presently serves as the Director of the Career Center at Westfield State University (MA) and has been in that role since 2009. Junior is also the The Washington Center Program Coordinator. As a first-generation college graduate and bilingual speaker, (English/Spanish), he has worked in higher education for over 20 years in career services and a short time in Admissions. He has been focused on serving student populations to achieve their goals over the course of his career. Junior recently completed a year long term as the President of the Eastern Association of Colleges and Employers (EACE): an organization dedicated to connecting career counseling professionals with the employer community. Additionally, over the last ten years he has served as the Executive Chair/President to the Massachusetts Educational Recruiting Consortium (MERC); an organization that facilitates hiring in Education. Contact Phone Number 413-572-5206 Location Parenzo Hall 130 Email jdelgado@westfield.ma.edu LinkedIn @juniordelgado Schedule an Appointment View Calendar 413-572-5206 Recent Posts Labor Market Insights Module Giselle Frechette Associate Director Giselle Frechette joined the Westfield State University Career Center in February 2007 and has over 20 years of experience in the field.  Giselle serves as the Disney College Program Advisor. As a first-generation college graduate, Giselle is committed to helping students navigate college, understand the various career pathways, and make professional connections to reach their personal and professional goals.  Her passion is helping students get connected to the right opportunities to find their life’s passion. If you have an opportunity for a student or a recent graduate, she’d love to connect you with the right candidate! Go Owls! Contact Phone Number 413-572-5206 Location Parenzo Hall 130 Email gfrechette@westfield.ma.edu LinkedIn @gisellefrechette Schedule an Appointment View Calendar 413-572-5206 Recent Posts Advice from Graduates (2:54) What I Wish I Knew (3:09) Early Career Programs & Internships for College Students Find Mentors Make Your Resume Pop (3:31) Dino Innarelli Assistant Director and Coordinator of Data Management and Alumni Career Services Dino joined the Career Center in 2010 with over twenty years of career advising and workforce development experience.  He manages the data collection, analysis, 